{"author":"lars@redhat.com","body":"Our current model requires a separate values file for each chart. It would be nice if the configuration for a cluster could be placed in a single file. This requires restructuring our charts so that instead of expecting values consisting of multiple top-level keys:\n\n```yaml\nnamespace: foo\noperatorgroup:\n  targetNamespaces: false\n```\n\nWe would place all the values for a chart under a top-level key named after the chart:\n\n```yaml\nfoo-chart:\n  namespace: foo\n  operatorgroup:\n    targetNamespaces: false\n```\n\nThis would allow combining the values for multiple charts in a single file:\n\n```yaml\nfoo-chart:\n  namespace: foo\n  operatorgroup:\n    targetNamespaces: false\n\nbar-chart:\n  namespace: bar\n  externalSecretName: bar-secret\n```\n\nThis would allow us to transform this:\n\n```\nvalues/oac-prod-infra/oac-prod-workload0/\n├── cert-manager.yaml\n├── cluster-certificates.yaml\n├── external-secrets.yaml\n├── metallb.yaml\n├── object-storage-proxy.yaml\n├── portworx.yaml\n├── rhoai.yaml\n└── user-projects.yaml\n```\n\nInto this:\n\n```\nvalues/oac-prod-infra/oac-prod-workload0/\n└── values.yaml\n```"}